    {
      "title": "National Rally’s Jordan Bardella rails at ‘war’ on party after antisemitism claims",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/29/jordan-bardella-national-rally-antisemitism-claims-france",
      "description": "<p>President of Marine Le Pen’s far-right party faces calls to resign over comments he allegedly wrote as a teenager</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/may/01/a-paradigm-shift-will-jordan-bardella-finally-normalise-le-pens-far-right\">Jordan Bardella</a>, the head of Marine Le Pen’s far-right National Rally (RN), has claimed a “total war” is being waged against his party as he faces a political storm after the publication of antisemitic comments he allegedly wrote as a young party member.</p><p>Bardella, who is facing calls from political opponents to resign, said on Tuesday that the <a href=\"https://www.mediapart.fr/journal/politique/280926/les-banques-sont-toutes-detenues-par-des-juifs-jordan-bardella-face-ses-ecrits-antisemites\">report by the investigative website Mediapart</a> was false. To a standing ovation from his party’s lawmakers and senators at a meeting in parliament, he said the report was an attempt to damage his party as Le Pen tops the polls before the 2027 presidential election.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/29/jordan-bardella-national-rally-antisemitism-claims-france\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-29T15:16:39"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accusations of Antisemitism Hit a Star of the French Far Right",
